# Git and Dependencies

## Git

- Do not force-push. Do not rewrite Git history unless explicitly requested.
- Do not delete branches without approval.
- Do not commit generated folders such as `.next`, build output, caches, or `node_modules` unless the project explicitly requires them.
- Before major changes, verify the current branch and working tree.
- Keep commits logical and reversible. Only commit when the user asks.

## Dependencies

- Do not install packages unless they are actually needed.
- Before installing a package, check whether the existing stack already provides the required functionality.
- Prefer stable, well-maintained packages compatible with the project's current Next.js / React / Node versions.
- Avoid unnecessary dependencies. Do not upgrade major versions automatically.
